  "title": "Draft Neanderthal genome published",
  "summary": "On 7 May 2010 Science published a draft sequence of the Neandertal genome, built by a team at the Max Planck Institute for Evolutionary Anthropology in Leipzig from DNA of three individuals, covering over four billion bases. It found that Neandertals shared more variants with present-day Eurasians than with sub-Saharan Africans, which the institute reported as evidence of interbreeding.",
